    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does LinkedIn personal branding work for a consulting partner or PE/VC principal in Bengaluru?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">For a Partner, Principal, Senior Manager, MD/GM at Big-4 (McKinsey + BCG + Bain + Kearney + Big-4 consulting arms) + PE/VC (Peak XV + Sequoia + Blackstone + KKR + ChrysCapital + India-focused VCs) in Bengaluru, LinkedIn is your practice-building + client-BD + industry-positioning engine. ITD runs your LinkedIn: optimised About Us (practice + industry-focus + credentials + firm) + featured section (whitepapers + speaking engagements + published articles), 2-4 weekly posts (industry frameworks + trend analysis + deal-commentary on public transactions + hiring + team + firm), 1-2 long-form articles/month, Creator Mode + newsletter (extremely powerful for consulting audience), engagement + community management, LinkedIn Live for major industry themes. Consulting + PE/VC is LinkedIn's most credentials-driven segment. Senior consultants + partners use LinkedIn for practice-building + client-BD + industry positioning + hiring + fund-raising (VC associates + partners). Peer competition + credibility signalling extreme.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic monthly retainer for LinkedIn personal branding for a Bengaluru consulting partner or PE/VC principal?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In Bengaluru: Rs 40,000-3 lakh. Starter (Rs 50-95K) — profile + 8-12 posts/month + 1 article + community + analytics. Growth (Rs 95K-2L) — full Creator Mode + newsletter + video + LinkedIn Live + BD + speaking-invitations advisory. Enterprise (Rs 2.2-4L) — partner-level content ops with heavy speaking + PR + industry-committee + firm-BD integration. Compare against 1 senior consultant/partner retained on LinkedIn drives Rs 5-50 crore in practice-attributed engagements + firm-BD over 24-36 months — 15-60x agency-retainer ROI — retainer pays back inside 2-4 weeks of first LinkedIn-attributed engagement.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What compliance + client-confidentiality rules apply to a consultant's LinkedIn content?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Client-confidentiality strict (never disclose engagement details without written permission) + M&A/deal-adjacent content requires NDA compliance + partner-approval for public sharing. Practically: (1) NEVER share engagement details without written client permission + firm approval (breach of NDA is career-ending), (2) M&A + deal-adjacent content restricted during transaction (SEBI + insider-trading concerns), (3) Public deals can be commented on 60-90 days post-close with attribution-free framing, (4) Industry frameworks + trend analysis + market data (public sources) are always safe, (5) Client-stories require signed release from client + firm approval, (6) Speaking + whitepaper + published-article content can freely be amplified. ITD compliance-review workflow prevents accidental disclosure.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What content should a Bengaluru consulting partner or PE/VC principal publish on LinkedIn?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Industry frameworks + trend analysis + M&A/deal commentary (public deals) + hiring + team + client-story-with-consent + speaking engagements + whitepaper + industry-body engagement. Winning mix: 30-35% industry framework + strategy + trend analysis (your practice area), 20-25% deal + M&A commentary on public transactions (add insight + context — never insider info), 15-20% hiring + firm + team + promotion announcements (peer-recognition + firm-BD), 10-15% speaking + whitepaper + conference-recap + industry-body engagement, 10-15% market data + industry reports (repost with your added commentary), 5-10% personal + firm-culture + long-form essays. In Bengaluru, Big-4 partners + PE/VC principals build followership through frameworks + industry-thesis content.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How much engagement + follower growth for a Bengaluru consulting partner or PE/VC principal?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Month 1-3: 500-1,500 new followers, 8-15% engagement, 20-80 profile views/day. Month 3-6: 1,500-4,000 followers, 50-200 profile views/day, first inbound client + speaking DMs. Month 6-12: 4,000-15,000 followers, 200-1,000 profile views/day, 10-40 qualified BD DMs/month, 3-15 speaking + advisory + engagement inquiries/month. Month 12+: compounding — consulting/PE partners often hit 30K-100K+ followers by year 2-3 with consistent thought-leadership. Peer benchmark: India's leading consulting partners + PE principals (McKinsey/BCG/Bain/Peak XV senior team) have 40K-500K+ followers.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we drive inbound client + speaking + advisory enquiries via LinkedIn?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Five channels: (1) Optimised About Us + featured section clearly signalling practice-focus + industry-expertise + deal-attribution (public deals) + speaking history, (2) Weekly framework + trend content that ranks in LinkedIn Search for your practice area — clients search 'best consulting partner for retail digital transformation' + 'India PE partner focused on SaaS', (3) LinkedIn newsletter (consulting + PE audience subscribes heavily to thought-leader newsletters), (4) LinkedIn Live for major industry themes — drives speaking + advisory + engagement inbound, (5) Strategic engagement on other partners + CXOs + policy-maker content.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we position deal-attribution content without violating NDA?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Best-practice framework: (1) Public deals only (announced + closed + press-released), (2) 60-90 days post-close before commentary, (3) Focus on industry-implications + strategic-rationale + market-context (not confidential details), (4) Attribution to firm + your role (with firm approval), (5) Learnings + framework + generalisable insight rather than transaction-specific detail, (6) Firm compliance officer sign-off if role involves regulated M&A/PE deals. This mirrors how partners at McKinsey + BCG + Bain + Peak XV commentate on Reliance/Tata/Adani deals — attributable + insight-driven + compliance-safe.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Should a consulting partner or PE/VC principal post daily?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Not daily — 3-4 high-quality posts/week + 1-2 long-form articles/month + occasional LinkedIn Live outperforms daily posting. Consulting/PE audience values depth + insight over volume. Daily-posting often reads as insecure or brand-focused rather than substance-focused. In Bengaluru, top-tier consulting partners + PE principals typically post 12-16 pieces/month + 2-3 long-form articles/quarter + occasional LinkedIn Live + 100+ substantive comments/month.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What if my firm has restrictions on partners' LinkedIn activity?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Standard at large consulting + PE/VC firms. Two paths: (1) Firm-brand-aligned personal LinkedIn with firm's marketing + compliance review pre-publish, (2) Personal thought-leadership on industry frameworks + trends that respect firm brand + never disclose engagement details. Firms like McKinsey + BCG + Bain + Peak XV + Sequoia have specific partner-LinkedIn playbooks — ITD works within your firm's framework or advises on optimal engagement path. In Bengaluru, senior partners at Big-4 + top PE firms increasingly build strong personal LinkedIn presence within firm-approved boundaries.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we track LinkedIn ROI for a Bengaluru consulting partner or PE/VC principal?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Weekly: profile views + newsletter subscribers + post engagement + inbound DMs from CXOs + saved content + speaking-invitation inbound. Monthly: qualified BD DMs + booked meetings + LinkedIn-attributed engagement inquiries + speaking + panel invitations + industry-body engagement + hiring-attributed to LinkedIn. Quarterly: LinkedIn-attributed practice growth + engagement-revenue + speaking-honorarium + firm-BD-attributed. Realistic: 3-6 months for first meaningful attribution (longer than SaaS because consulting/PE buyer takes more time to research + engage) + 12-24 months for major compounding + full ROI clarity.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does ITD's LinkedIn service for consulting differ from a generic content agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Consulting/PE-native writer team: we understand strategy frameworks, M&A dynamics, PE deal-structuring, fund-life-cycle, industry-specific consulting practice. (2) Ghost-writing quality: our writing passes for partner-level thought leadership (Big-4 partners + PE principals routinely use ghost-writing — voice-capture makes it authentic). (3) Compliance + NDA workflow built-in — we never violate client confidentiality. (4) Industry-framework + market-data content capacity: we can synthesise Deloitte/PwC/EY/McKinsey/BCG public research + your own insight. (5) LinkedIn newsletter + Live + long-form specialisation. (6) Founder + senior-partner team on your account (not junior social manager).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we start LinkedIn personal branding with ITD as a Bengaluru consulting partner or PE/VC principal?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Free 30-min discovery call. We audit your current LinkedIn + benchmark against 3-5 competing partners at your firm-tier in Bengaluru/India + share customised 90-day plan + tier recommendation within 3 working days. If you proceed: 1-week onboarding (60-90 min voice-capture on practice + industry-thesis + firm-compliance-alignment + content-approval workflow) + first content live in week 2. Under NDA if required — we routinely work with senior consulting + PE partners under strict confidentiality.</div>
